            "single",
            "blank",
            "open"
        ],
        "answer": [
            "(C) Analog-to-Digital Conversion (ADC)",
            "30 ns",
            "The residue amplifier amplifies the difference between the actual analog input and its quantized digital representation to improve conversion accuracy in subsequent stages."
        ],
        "explanation": [
            "The primary function of the ADC is to convert analog signals into digital signals, which is the fundamental operation of an Analog-to-Digital Converter.",
            "t0 is the sum of t1, t2, and t3 according to the timing diagram, which is 5 ns + 10 ns + 15 ns = 30 ns.",
            "The residue amplifier serves to amplify the residuals of the conversion errors from one stage before moving to the next conversion stage, ensuring improved accuracy of the ADC over multiple pipelined stages."
        ],
