    "spec_98": {
        "statement": "Based on the specification document for the TPA31xxD2 family of electronic devices, answer the following questions related to electronic design automation (EDA).",
        "question": [
            "1. Identify the recommended R1 resistor value for setting a gain of 32 dB in Master mode from Table 1. (A) 5.6 k\u03a9 (B) 39 k\u03a9 (C) 47 k\u03a9 (D) 100 k\u03a9",
            "2. From the schematic in Figure 27, how many distinct PVCC decoupling capacitors are recommended for each amplifier channel?",
            "3. Calculate the high-pass filter cut-off frequency for a 32 dB gain using the formula provided, given that the input capacitance is 5.6 \u03bcF and input impedance is 15 k\u03a9. Provide the result in Hertz, rounded to the nearest tenth."
        ],
        "question_type": [
            "single",
            "blank",
            "open"
        ],
        "answer": [
            "(B) 39 k\u03a9",
            "3",
            "1.9 Hz"
        ],
        "explanation": [
            "The document lists 39 k\u03a9 as the recommended R1 value for a 32 dB gain in Master mode.",
            "Reviewing the schematic in Figure 27 shows each channel needs three PVCC decoupling capacitors.",
            "The high-pass filter cut-off frequency is calculated using the formula f = 1 / (2\u03c0Z_iC_i), substituting Z_i = 15,000 \u03a9 and C_i = 5.6\u00d710^-6 F. This yields approximately 1.9 Hz."
        ],
