    "spec_99": {
        "statement": "Based on the specification document of the TPA31xxD2 amplifier, answer the following questions.",
        "question": [
            "Which condition triggers the 'Over Temperature' fault in the TPA31xxD2 amplifier? \n(A) Tj > 150\u00b0C \n(B) Tj < 100\u00b0C \n(C) PVCC < 4.5V \n(D) DC output voltage",
            "Describe the purpose of the PLIMIT feature in the TPA31xxD2 amplifier.",
            "Calculate the output power (P_OUT) if the following parameters are given: R_L = 4\u03a9, R_S = 0.1\u03a9, Vp = 3V."
        ],
        "question_type": [
            "single",
            "open",
            "blank"
        ],
        "answer": [
            "A",
            "The PLIMIT feature is used to limit the output peak-to-peak voltage, effectively reducing the power consumption by simulating a lower supply voltage.",
            "P_OUT = 3.24 W"
        ],
        "explanation": [
            "The 'Over Temperature' fault is triggered when the junction temperature (Tj) exceeds 150\u00b0C, as specified in the fault reporting table.",
            "The document highlights that the PLIMIT feature limits the duty cycle to a specific value, thus controlling the peak-to-peak output voltage to manage power output efficiently.",
            "Using the formula P_OUT = ((R_L / (R_L + 2 * R_S) * Vp)^2) / (2 * R_L), substitute R_L = 4\u03a9, R_S = 0.1\u03a9, Vp = 3V: P_OUT = ((4 / (4 + 0.2) * 3)^2) / (2 * 4) = 3.24 W."
        ],
        "difficulty": [
            "easy",
            "medium",
            "hard"
        ],
        "ability": [
            "perception",
            "inference",
            "computation"
        ],
        "ic_type": "analog",
