    "spec_111": {
        "statement": "You are given a list of pages extracted from the specification document of an electronic device. The content of the pages is:\nRev. 3.1\n2/2011\nPage 5 of 18\nV\u2022I CHIP CORP. (A VICOR COMPANY) 25 FRONTAGE RD. ANDOVER, MA 01810  800-735-6200\nvicorpower.com \nx 020\n080A00\ny\nE\n48\nVTM\n5.0 APPLICATION CHARACTERISTICS\nThe following values, typical of an application environment, are collected at TC = 25\u00baC unless otherwise noted. See associated figures\nfor general trend data.\nATTRIBUTE\nSYMBOL\nCONDITIONS / NOTES\nTYP\nUNIT\nNo load power dissipation\nPNL\nVIN = 48 V, PC enabled\n4.4\nW\nEfficiency (ambient)\n\u03b7AMB\nVIN = 48 V, IOUT = 80 A\n92.1\n%\nEfficiency (hot)\n\u03b7HOT\nVIN = 48 V, IOUT = 80 A, TC = 100\u00baC\n91.7\n%\nOutput resistance (cold)\nROUT_COLD\nVIN = 48 V, IOUT = 80 A, TC = -40\u00baC\n0.8\nm\u03a9\nOutput resistance (ambient)\nROUT_AMB\nVIN = 48 V, IOUT = 80 A\n1.1\nm\u03a9\nOutput resistance (hot)\nROUT_HOT\nVIN = 48 V, IOUT = 80 A, TC = 100\u00baC\n1.4\nm\u03a9\nOutput voltage ripple\nVOUT_PP\nCOUT = 0 F, IOUT = 80 A, VIN = 48 V, \n279\nmV\n20 MHz BW, Section 12\nVOUT transient (positive)\nVOUT_TRAN+\nIOUT_STEP = 0 A TO 80A, VIN = 48 V,\n30\nmV\nISLEW = 19 A /us\nVOUT transient (negative)\nVOUT_TRAN-\nIOUT_STEP = 80 A to 0 A, VIN = 48 V\n110\nmV\nISLEW = 59 A /us\n1 \n3 \n5 \n7 \n9 \n11 \n26 \n29 \n32 \n35 \n38 \n41 \n43 \n46 \n49 \n52 \n55 \nInput Voltage (V)\nNo Load Power Dissipation (W)\n-40\u00b0C\n25\u00b0C\n100\u00b0C\nT       :\nCASE\nNo Load Power Dissipation vs. Line  \nFull Load Efficiency vs. Case Temperature\nCase Temperature (\u00b0C)\nFull Load Efficiency (%)\n26 V\n48 V\n55 V\nV  :\nIN\n86 \n88 \n90 \n92 \n94 \n-40 \n-20 \n0 \n20 \n40 \n60 \n80 \n100 \nEfficiency & Power Dissipation -40\u00b0C Case\nLoad Current (A)\nEfficiency (%)\n26 V\n48 V\n55 V\nV  :\nIN\n26 V\n48 V\n55 V\nPower Dissipation (W)\nPD\n\u03b7\n0 \n5 \n10 \n15 \n20 \n25 \n30 \n35 \n40 \n45 \n60 \n64 \n68 \n72 \n76 \n80 \n84 \n88 \n92 \n96 \n0 \n8 \n16 \n24 \n32 \n40 \n48 \n56 \n64 \n72 \n80 \n \nEfficiency & Power Dissipation 25\u00b0C Case  \nLoad Current (A)\nEfficiency (%)\n26 V\n48 V\n55 V\nV  :\nIN\n26 V\n48 V\n55 V\nPower Dissipation (W)\n\u03b7\nPD\n0 \n4 \n8 \n12 \n16 \n20 \n24 \n28 \n68 \n72 \n76 \n80 \n84 \n88 \n92 \n96 \n0 \n8 \n16 \n24 \n32 \n40 \n48 \n56 \n64 \n72 \n80 \n \nFigure 1 \u2013 No load power dissipation vs. VIN\nFigure 2 \u2013 Full load efficiency vs. temperature\nFigure 3 \u2013 Efficiency and power dissipation at \u201340\u00b0C\nFigure 4 \u2013 Efficiency and power dissipation at 25\u00b0C\n\nRev. 3.1\n2/2011\nPage 6 of 18\nV\u2022I CHIP CORP. (A VICOR COMPANY) 25 FRONTAGE RD. ANDOVER, MA 01810  800-735-6200\nvicorpower.com \nx 020\n080A00\ny\nE\n48\nVTM\nFigure 10 \u2013Start up from application of VIN; VC pre-applied\nCOUT = 27000 \u00b5F\nSafe Operating Area\nOutput Voltage (V)\nOutput Current (A)\n0 \n20 \n40 \n60 \n80 \n100 \n120 \n140 \n0 \n0.5 \n1 \n1.5 \n2 \n2.5 \n3 \n10 ms Max\nContinuous \nFigure 8 \u2013 Safe operating area\nFigure 9 \u2013 Full load ripple, 100 \u00b5F CIN; No external COUT.\nBoard mounted module, scope setting : 20 MHz analog BW\nLoad Current (A)\nRipple (mV pk-pk)\n26 V\n48 V\n55 V\nV   :\nIN\nOutput Voltage Ripple vs. Load\n50 \n75 \n100 \n125 \n150 \n175 \n200 \n225 \n250 \n275 \n300 \n0 \n8 \n16 \n24 \n32 \n40 \n48 \n56 \n64 \n72 \n80 \nFigure 7 \u2013 VRIPPLE vs. IOUT ; No external COUT.\nBoard mounted module, scope setting : 20 MHz analog BW\nEfficiency & Power Dissipation 100\u00b0C Case  \nLoad Current (A)\nEfficiency (%)\n26 V\n48 V\n55 V\nV  :\nIN\n26 V\n48 V\n55 V\nPower Dissipation (W)\nPD\n\u03b7\n0 \n4 \n8 \n12 \n16 \n20 \n24 \n28 \n68 \n72 \n76 \n80 \n84 \n88 \n92 \n96 \n0 \n8 \n16 \n24 \n32 \n40 \n48 \n56 \n64 \n72 \n80 \n \nROUT vs. TCASE at VIN = 48 V\nCase Temperature (\u00b0C)\n Rout (m\u03a9)\nI      :\nOUT\n40A\n80A\n0.0 \n0.5 \n1.0 \n1.5 \n2.0 \n-40 \n-20 \n0 \n20 \n40 \n60 \n80 \n100 \nFigure 5 \u2013 Efficiency and power dissipation at 100\u00b0C\nFigure 6 \u2013 ROUT vs. temperature\n\nRev. 3.1\n2/2011\nPage 7 of 18\nV\u2022I CHIP CORP. (A VICOR COMPANY) 25 FRONTAGE RD. ANDOVER, MA 01810  800-735-6200\nvicorpower.com \nx 020\n080A00\ny\nE\n48\nVTM\nFigure 13 \u2013 80 A \u2013 0 A transient response: \nCIN = 100 \u00b5F, no external COUT\nFigure 12 \u2013 0 A\u2013 80 A transient response:\nCIN = 100 \u00b5F, no external COUT\nFigure 11 \u2013 Start up from application of VC; VIN pre-applied \nCOUT = 27000 \u00b5F\n\nBased on the provided specification document for the electronic device, answer the following questions.",
        "question": [
            "What is the value of the TM fault response time (T_FR_TM) as per the datasheet? (A) 5 \u03bcs (B) 10 \u03bcs (C) 15 \u03bcs (D) 20 \u03bcs",
            "Identify the maxmium peak-to-peak ripple voltage (V_TM_PP) value given the conditions C_TM = 0 F, V_IN = 48 V, I_OUT = 80 A.",
            "Calculate the power dissipation (P_D) at 25\u00b0C if V_IN = 48 V, I_OUT = 80 A, and efficiency is 91.7%."
        ],
        "question_type": [
            "single",
            "blank",
            "open"
        ],
        "answer": [
            "(B) 10 \u03bcs",
            "200 mV",
            "4.42 W"
        ],
        "explanation": [
            "The TM fault response time (T_FR_TM) is listed as 10 \u03bcs in the specification under the TM capacitance (external) heading.",
            "The maxmium peak-to-peak ripple voltage (V_TM_PP) is provided directly as 200 mV in the table under ANALOG OUTPUT for the given conditions.",
            "The power dissipation (P_D) can be calculated using P_D = (1 - Efficiency) * Power Input. Given efficiency = 91.7%, V_IN = 48 V, I_OUT = 80 A, Power Input = V_IN * I_OUT = 3840 W. Therefore, P_D = (1 - 0.917) * 3840 = 4.42 W."
        ],
