        "question_type": [
            "single",
            "open",
            "blank"
        ],
        "answer": [
            "B",
            "Figure 7 illustrates the HPD timing during an auto switch scenario where the HPD is high for at least one other port. Initially, a selected port is active, followed by t2 (2s) where the channels switch to Hi-Z state. This is followed by t3 (1s) where a new selected port becomes active.",
            "2 seconds"
        ],
        "explanation": [
            "The propagation delay of HPDx Deserton is observed in Figure 7 according to the document.",
            "The explanation is based on the diagram description provided in Figure 7, which shows the timing switches and durations between different states.",
            "The total time is the sum of typical values for HPD_SRC low duration (1s) and HPDx assertion (1s), resulting in 3 seconds."
        ],
