        "question": [
            "What function does Pin 35 (LOCK) serve in the Genlock ADC? Select the correct answer: (A) Ground connection (B) Input for horizontal sync (C) High when Genlock is locked (D) No connection",
            "Given the electrical characteristics, if the typical dynamic power current (Icco) is 74mA and the supply voltage (VDD) is 5.25V, what is the typical power consumption of the ADC?",
            "Identify two pins related to the video signal and their descriptions from the pin description table."
        ],
        "question_type": [
            "single",
            "blank",
            "open"
        ],
        "answer": [
            "(C) High when Genlock is locked",
            "388.5 mW",
            "Pins 48 (CVBS0) and 49 (CVBS1) - 8 Bit Composite Video Baseband Signal"
        ],
        "explanation": [
            "Pin 35 (LOCK) is described as high when the Genlock is locked and in the tracking state.",
            "Power consumption is calculated by P = IV. Therefore, 74mA * 5.25V = 388.5 mW.",
            "Pins 48 to 55 are related to composite video baseband signals, as described in the pin description table."
        ],
