age for Analog Domain\n+ 5V Supply Voltage for Analog Domain\nGround\nNo Connection\nNo Connection\nLine Locked Horizontal Sync Signal\nNo Connection\nConnect this Pin to + 5V for proper Operation\n+ 5V Supply Voltage for Digital Domain\nGround\nFreq. & Phase compensated Sample Clock used for ADC\nConnect this Pin to + 5V for proper Operation\nNo Connection\nFrame Signal for Serial Data Interface\nNo Connection\nNo Connection\nNo Connection\nNo Connection\nNo Connection\nClock Signal Input for Serial Data Interface\nNo Connection\nSerial Data in Serial Interface\nNo Connection\nNo Connection\nNo Connection\nNo Connection\nNo Connection\nNo Connection\nNo Connection\nHigh when the GENLOCK is locked & in Tracking State\nNo Connection\nNo Connection\nNo Connection\nVertical Sync Signal Output\nSync level. Low when CVBS < 32. This Signal is not Line locked\n\nBased on the given specification document for the KS0118C integrated circuit, answer the following questions:",
        "question": [
            "What is the primary function of the KS0118C IC as described in the introduction? (A) Audio processing, (B) Video signal synchronization, (C) Temperature control",
            "Which component in the block diagram is directly responsible for reducing jitter? (A) CRYSTAL DRIVER, (B) JITTER REDUCTION, (C) DIGITAL OFFSET CONTROL, (D) SYNC DETECTOR",
            "Calculate the total differential phase error if the given differential phase is 2\u00b0 for five different inputs. Fill in the blank: Total differential phase error = _____\u00b0"
        ],
        "question_type": [
            "single",
            "single",
            "blank"
        ],
        "answer": [
            "(B) Video signal synchronization",
            "(B) JITTER REDUCTION",
            "10"
        ],
        "explanation": [
            "The introduction states that the KS0118C is used for gen lock and includes functions like digitization synchronized to video signals.",
            "The block diagram shows a component named JITTER REDUCTION, suggesting its purpose is to reduce jitter in signals.",
            "The differential phase error for one input is 2\u00b0, so for five inputs it is 5 * 2\u00b0 = 10\u00b0."
        ],
