e Sn control.\n\u2190\n3-STATE OUTPUT ENABLE/DISABLE TIMES\nBANK SKEW (where X denotes outputs in the same bank)\nXDP0:XDP9\nXDP0:XDP9\nSCOPE\nQx\nLVCMOS\nVDD\n GND\n This circuit is used for test purposes only,\nnot intended for application use.\n\nBased on the ICS83840B DDR SDRAM MUX specification documents, answer the following questions.",
        "question": [
            "What is the maximum switching speed of the ICS83840B DDR SDRAM MUX? (A) 1.5ns (B) 2ns (C) 3ns (D) 4ns",
            "If the nSx control input is set to H according to the function table, what can be inferred about the host port and DIMM port connection?",
            "Calculate the typical on-resistance R_on between the Host and the DIMM terminals when V_DD = 2.5V, V_A = 1.7V, and V_B = 1.5V."
        ],
        "question_type": [
            "single",
            "open",
            "blank"
        ],
        "answer": [
            "C",
            "The host port is disconnected and the DIMM port is connected to 400\u03a9 to GND.",
            "8"
        ],
        "explanation": [
            "The maximum switching speed is listed as 3ns in the Features section of the document.",
            "According to the function table, an nSx input of H means the Host Port is disconnected and the DIMM Port is 400\u03a9 to GND.",
            "The typical on-resistance R_on for V_DD = 2.5V, V_A = 1.7V, and V_B = 1.5V is 8\u03a9 as given in Table 4B under 'DC Characteristics'."
        ],
