    "spec_145": {
        "statement": "You are given a list of pages extracted from the specification document of an electronic device. The content of the pages is:\nDAC 3550A\nMicronas\n29\nFig. 4\u20139: Application circuit schematic 2: MPEG application with analog Megabass and 14.725 MHz crystal\nn\nA\nA\n\nDAC 3550A\n30\nMicronas\n \nFig. 4\u201310: MPEG Layer-3 Player\nFig. 4\u201311: CD-Player with FM-Radio\nFig. 4\u201312: ADR Receiver\nMAS\nROM, CD-ROM, \nRAM, Flash Mem. ..\nDAC\nHost\n3507D\n3550A\n(PC, Controller)\nI2S\nline out\ndemand signal\nMPEG clock\nMPEG bit stream\n         CLKOUT\n14.725 MHz\nOptical \nDSP\nI2S\nline out\n         CLKOUT\nDAC\n3550A\nDAC\n3550A\n&\nSERVO\nPickup\nFM-TUNER\nDEMOD\nR\nL\n384 \u00d7 fs\n \nI2S\nline-out\nDAC\n3550A\nDAC\n3550A\nTUNER\nADRBUS\nDATA\nBCLK\nLRCLK\n32 kHz\n18.432 MHz\n18.432 MHz\nDRP\n3510 A\nMSP\n34xx\n\nDAC 3550A\nMicronas\n31\n\nBased on the given specification document of the DAC 3550A.",
        "question": [
            "Explain the role of the Megabass circuit in the context of the DAC 3550A application.",
            "Calculate the total resistance seen at the LINE-Out-Right if the resistors connected in series are 15K ohm and 82 ohm."
        ],
        "question_type": [
            "open",
            "blank"
        ],
        "answer": [
            "The Megabass circuit enhances low-frequency audio signals by amplifying them, thus improving sound quality.",
            "15082"
        ],
        "explanation": [
            "The Megabass circuit amplifies low-frequency audio signals, providing a richer and deeper sound output.",
            "The resistors connected in series can be added up to compute the total resistance: 15000 ohms + 82 ohms = 15082 ohms."
        ],
        "difficulty": [
            "medium",
