n\u00b1IPD\n80\n100\n120\n\u00b5A\nA\n6.3\nOutput current B71 to \nB70 = \u201c10\u201d\nPD = 2.5V\n2\n\u00b1IPD\n400\n500\n600\n\u00b5A\nA\n6.4\nOutput current B71 to \nB70 = \u201c11\u201d\nPD = 2.5V\n2\n\u00b1IPD\n1500\n2000\n2400\n\u00b5A\nA\n6.5\nLeakage current\nPD = 2.5V\n2\n\u00b1IPDL\n20\nnA\nA\n7\nPDO\n7.1\nSaturation voltage \nHIGH \n3, 4\n8.0\n8.5\nV\nA\n7.2\nSaturation voltage \nLOW\n3, 4\n0\n0.4\nV\nA\n8\nSWO1, SWO2, SWO3, SWO4 (Open Drain)\n8.1\nOutput leakage current \nHIGH\nPin 7, 8, 9, 10 over R \nagainst 8.5V\n7, 8, \n9, 10\nISWOH\n100\nnA\nA\n8.2\nOutput voltage LOW\nI = 1 mA\n7, 8, \n9, 10\nVSWOL\n100\n400\nmV\nA\n9\nDAC1, DAC2\n9.1\nOutput current\n3, 4\nIDAC1, 2\n1\nmA\nC\n9.2\nOutput voltage\n3, 4\nVDAC1, 2\n0.3\nVS \u2013 \n0.6\nV\nA\n9.3\nMaximum offset range \n(FM)\nOffset = 0, Gain = 53\n3, 4\n0.45\n0.56\n0.65\nV\nA\n9.4\nMinimum offset range \n(FM)\nOffset = 63, Gain = 53\n3, 4\n\u20130.45\n\u20130.57\n\u20130.65\nV\nA\n*) Type means: A = 100% tested, B = 100% correlation tested, C = Characterized on samples, D = Design parameter\n\nBased on the ATR4256 specification document, answer the following questions regarding the 3-wire bus timing diagram and control registers.",
        "question": [
            "What is the function of the R-Divider in the control register table? (A) To divide the clock frequency. (B) To filter the input signal. (C) To adjust voltage levels. (D) To store data temporarily.",
            "Refer to Figure 6-1: What is the purpose of the t_HDA time period in the 3-wire bus timing diagram?",
            "Calculate the maximum frequency of the input signal (f_in) if the programmable N, R divider SF is set to its minimum value. Provide your answer in MHz."
        ],
        "question_type": [
            "single",
            "open",
            "blank"
        ],
        "answer": [
            "(A)",
            "The t_HDA time period compensates for the hold time required for stable data transfer.",
            "160"
        ],
        "explanation": [
            "The R-Divider is used to divide the clock frequency as per the control register configuration.",
            "The t_HDA is set to ensure that there is sufficient hold time for the data after the clock signal, preventing data loss or corruption.",
            "The maximum frequency when SF is at its minimum (2) is calculated based on the f_in value given as 160 MHz."
        ],
