    "spec_161": {
        "statement": "You are given a list of pages extracted from the specification document of an electronic device. The content of the pages is:\nV\nVV\nVVolta\nolta\nolta\nolta\noltagggggeeeee\nComparator\nComparator\nComparator\nComparator\nComparator\nAS111\nAustin Semiconductor, Inc. reserves the right to change products or specifications without notice.\n14\nAS111\nRev. 1.6 6/05\nAustin Semiconductor, Inc.\nTYPICAL APPLICATIONS (Pin numbers refer to TO08 can package)(Continued)\n\nV\nVV\nVVolta\nolta\nolta\nolta\noltagggggeeeee\nComparator\nComparator\nComparator\nComparator\nComparator\nAS111\nAustin Semiconductor, Inc. reserves the right to change products or specifications without notice.\n15\nAS111\nRev. 1.6 6/05\nAustin Semiconductor, Inc.\nSCHEMATIC DIAGRAM20\nNOTE 20: Pin connections shown on schematic diagram are for the TO08 can package.\n\nV\nVV\nVVolta\nolta\nolta\nolta\noltagggggeeeee\nComparator\nComparator\nComparator\nComparator\nComparator\nAS111\nAustin Semiconductor, Inc. reserves the right to change products or specifications without notice.\n16\nAS111\nRev. 1.6 6/05\nAustin Semiconductor, Inc.\nASI Case (Package Designator C008)\nSMD 5962-86877, Case Outline P\nMECHANICAL DEFINITIONS*\n*All measurements are in inches.\nMIN\nMAX\nA\n---\n0.200\nb\n0.014\n0.026\nb2\n0.045\n0.065\nc\n0.008\n0.018\nD\n---\n0.405\nE\n0.220\n0.310\ne\neA\nL\n0.125\n0.200\nQ\n0.015\n0.060\nS1\n0.005\n---\nS2\n0.005\n---\nSYMBOL\nASI SPECIFICATIONS\n0.100 BCS\n0.300 BSC\n\nBased on the provided schematic and application diagrams for the AS111 Voltage Comparator, answer the following questions.",
        "question": [
            "According to the schematic diagram on page 15, which pin is connected to the positive voltage supply? (A) Pin 1 (B) Pin 2 (C) Pin 3 (D) Pin 4",
            "Using the typical application diagram on page 13, what is the purpose of R2 in the Precision Photodiode Comparator circuit? Explain your reasoning.",
            "Calculate the total resistance in series with the input in the Switching Power Amplifier circuit on page 14 when a reference resistor R7 of 15k\u03a9 is used."
