    "spec_162": {
        "statement": "You are given a list of pages extracted from the specification document of an electronic device. The content of the pages is:\nV\nVV\nVVolta\nolta\nolta\nolta\noltagggggeeeee\nComparator\nComparator\nComparator\nComparator\nComparator\nAS111\nAustin Semiconductor, Inc. reserves the right to change products or specifications without notice.\n11\nAS111\nRev. 1.6 6/05\nAustin Semiconductor, Inc.\nTYPICAL APPLICATIONS (Pin numbers refer to TO08 can package)(Continued)\n\nV\nVV\nVVolta\nolta\nolta\nolta\noltagggggeeeee\nComparator\nComparator\nComparator\nComparator\nComparator\nAS111\nAustin Semiconductor, Inc. reserves the right to change products or specifications without notice.\n12\nAS111\nRev. 1.6 6/05\nAustin Semiconductor, Inc.\nTYPICAL APPLICATIONS (Pin numbers refer to TO08 can package)(Continued)\n\nV\nVV\nVVolta\nolta\nolta\nolta\noltagggggeeeee\nComparator\nComparator\nComparator\nComparator\nComparator\nAS111\nAustin Semiconductor, Inc. reserves the right to change products or specifications without notice.\n13\nAS111\nRev. 1.6 6/05\nAustin Semiconductor, Inc.\nTYPICAL APPLICATIONS (Pin numbers refer to TO08 can package)(Continued)\n\nBased on the given pages from the AS111 voltage comparator specification document, answer the following questions.",
        "question": [
            "Which component is used to improve response speed in the 'Using Clamp Diodes to Improve Response' application? (A) Resistor (B) Diode (C) Capacitor (D) Inductor",
            "Explain how the AS111 is used in a crystal oscillator circuit.",
            "Calculate the frequency of the voltage-controlled oscillator circuit if C1 is 1.5 \u00b5F."
        ],
        "question_type": [
            "single",
            "open",
            "blank"
        ],
        "answer": [
            "B",
            "In the crystal oscillator application, the AS111 is used to maintain a stable frequency by acting as an amplifier with feedback. The crystal provides a stable oscillation frequency, which is amplified by the AS111, ensuring a consistent output frequency.",
            "f = 1061.55 Hz"
        ],
        "explanation": [
            "The circuit uses diodes to clamp and improve the response speed by limiting voltage spikes.",
            "The crystal sets the frequency, and the AS111 amplifies this signal, allowing for a consistent output signal to be generated.",
            "To calculate the frequency: f = 1 / (2 * \u03c0 * R * C). For R_tot = 1k\u03a9 (simplified), f = 1 / (2 * \u03c0 * 1k\u03a9 * 1.5e-6 F) \u2248 1061.55 Hz."
        ],
