nN/A\n1700\nTRENCH 3\n30\n2.0\nSP3\nYES\nAPTGT30H170T3G\nN/A\n50\n2.0\nSP4\nYES\nAPTGT50H170TG\nAPTGT50DH170TG\n100\n2.0\nSP6\n-\nAPTGT100H170G\nAPTGT100DH170G\n150\n2.0\nSP6\n-\nAPTGT150H170G\nAPTGT150DH170G\nFULL & ASYMMETRICAL BRIDGE\nNEW!\nNEW!\nSP4\nNEW!\nNEW!\nNEW!\n\nBased on the IGBT power modules specification pages, answer the following questions:",
        "question": [
            "What is the package type used for IGBT modules with a Vces of 600V and trench technology? (A) SP1 (B) SP3 (C) SP6 (D) D1",
            "How does the IGBT type affect the maximum current rating at Tj = 80\u00b0C according to the document?",
            "Calculate the total number of different packages used for IGBT modules across all listed types and configurations."
        ],
        "question_type": [
            "single",
            "open",
            "blank"
        ],
        "answer": [
            "A",
            "The IGBT type influences the maximum current (Ic) by allowing different current levels depending on its construction. For instance, trench types generally allow a higher current than NPT types.",
            "10"
        ],
        "explanation": [
            "The package type SP1 is predominantly used for 600V trench technology modules as seen in the specification tables.",
            "Different IGBT types, such as NPT and trench, have varying structural characteristics affecting their thermal and electrical performance, leading to different current ratings.",
            "By listing and counting all unique package types mentioned across the pages, we arrive at a total of 10 unique packages."
        ],
